{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792482544,"nonce":"K4P4D2koRo8kewDvKIvCT98MOl0=","message":"The initial static zyntax_ts/zynode foundation and oracle harness are ready, but this parent remains open. Six pinned expected gaps are inferred function return types, unions, generics, arrays, closures and structural width views. Additional unimplemented constructs include classes, optional/null representations, multi-file/module linking, reference-valued fields and cycles, complete JS coercion/string semantics and Node console formatting. Functions capturing module lexical bindings still need closure/global binding support. The upstream smoke sample immediately encounters var hoisting, enum and ambient declaration support; these are implementation work, not permanent restrictions or opt-out soundness decisions.\n\nKeep TypeScript-compatible assignment as the default and additional checks opt-in. Readonly weakening is currently tested at initialization, assignment, call, return, assertion, inferred bindings and non-null wrappers. Before async functions are enabled, audit the existing separate DynamicValue-to-pointer native trampoline: the synchronous float-entry ABI fix does not redesign it. Continue extending the upstream driver rather than treating skipped/malformed/unsupported tests as passes. Native graph ownership and any future collector policy require separate design; the current scalar-record frontend leaves GC disabled.","files":null}]}